#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c81626a0-6613-5f5d-9dda-df853958c571" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c50b2be-602c-50a5-ab71-1319601cdfad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-3s}{(s-1)(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c50b2be-602c-50a5-ab71-1319601cdfad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-3s}{(s-1)(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458764} :answer-field/id #uuid "faed85bb-89ce-5a06-b08b-d84b4c3cd7a9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164004} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75b58a4a-5911-578a-866b-5d33776cf35d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75b58a4a-5911-578a-866b-5d33776cf35d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458835} :answer-field/id #uuid "18a50378-7dea-5125-b1f1-8186b60315c8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17eee175-34bb-5ca1-9aad-a080088cd275" :question/math-academy-id "q-322280" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1={X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+3=-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns{X}_{1}(s)-1={X}_{1}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{1}{s-1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns{X}_{2}(s)+3=-(\\frac{1}{s-1})+3{X}_{2}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-3s+2}{(s-1)(s-3)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c81626a0-6613-5f5d-9dda-df853958c571" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95d1ef6b-caf6-5764-bc12-294fa204246c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-4s-17}{(s-4)(s+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95d1ef6b-caf6-5764-bc12-294fa204246c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-4s-17}{(s-4)(s+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303387} :answer-field/id #uuid "518f0276-0f4b-5c49-a892-c180fc62763c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304299} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee8ef59c-2d4f-5cd8-bd73-bde62a85dcd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{s+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee8ef59c-2d4f-5cd8-bd73-bde62a85dcd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{s+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303953} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdcc71fe-ab2d-5096-8ba2-82ce4b706e91" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304592}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c4c84fb-7fb4-580a-bff4-417ed1ebd433" :question/math-academy-id "q-331918" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3=-2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+4=-3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get \n\n$$\ns{X}_{1}(s)-3=-2{X}_{1}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3}{s+2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s)$ gives\n\n$$\ns{X}_{2}(s)+4=-3(\\frac{3}{s+2})+4{X}_{2}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-4s-17}{(s-4)(s+2)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09ce315d-395c-57f6-9266-37e8d3f8b69c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09ce315d-395c-57f6-9266-37e8d3f8b69c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458636} :answer-field/id #uuid "3facc676-db7c-504b-ad37-cb6479ec45aa" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459119} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca4efff0-ed8b-5efd-baf0-8bedffbf9612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca4efff0-ed8b-5efd-baf0-8bedffbf9612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458986} :answer-field/id #uuid "4970ea8c-d3ed-5408-b30d-972d0f9f7a39" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "184e26b8-c664-56cb-af6b-ea4090d916b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "184e26b8-c664-56cb-af6b-ea4090d916b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458668} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8864a88-2dcd-5b4e-a2d6-71c37f0f4d96" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459157} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b34ae040-bdf3-5b46-a211-b8e15b7220a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b34ae040-bdf3-5b46-a211-b8e15b7220a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458951} :answer-field/id #uuid "af20bb90-cb1f-52c6-b8c0-17deb5f81cee" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2e221fc3-b674-5d25-8035-e02c5aeade93" :question/math-academy-id "q-332300" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{5}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{5}{s-2}+\\frac{2}{s+1}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{2t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{-t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{5}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =5\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\} \\\\  & =5{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =5{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{5}{s-2}+\\frac{2}{s+1}\\} \\\\  & =5\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-2}\\}+2\\,{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s+1}\\} \\\\  & =5{e}^{2\\cdot t}+2{e}^{-1\\cdot t} \\\\  & =5{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5{e}^{2t} \\\\ 5{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8489f83-40a0-5fa2-86f5-bd04c15c744a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8489f83-40a0-5fa2-86f5-bd04c15c744a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459034} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f1fd3da-f4de-532f-a46e-f3ecb6847ac3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459097} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a6d7c96-1bca-5bf1-899f-bcc0cdc4ebc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a6d7c96-1bca-5bf1-899f-bcc0cdc4ebc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458712} :answer-field/id #uuid "282aaf72-408c-5f10-8ec6-186aa6a44cdc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec06874d-7f4b-520f-b784-c3ff1e8d0cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec06874d-7f4b-520f-b784-c3ff1e8d0cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459043} :answer-field/id #uuid "346e7d15-351c-5545-950d-eeabcb321de2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459109} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "338cd1b7-92b2-52a0-8bfb-86cc6a89733e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "338cd1b7-92b2-52a0-8bfb-86cc6a89733e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458727} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e028d21-3f7c-5da7-8e50-d18b331f55cd" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26b8e713-769d-5a04-9ac2-84441f94ba94" :question/math-academy-id "q-332395" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{3}{s}+\\frac{2}{s-3},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{3t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3}{s}+\\frac{2}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+2{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =3+2{e}^{3t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}-{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1-{e}^{3\\cdot t} \\\\  & =3-{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 3-{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3db932f4-fae5-50c6-9f86-537475346704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3db932f4-fae5-50c6-9f86-537475346704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302842} :answer-field/id #uuid "51f9ccbb-98c5-5a7d-8a34-9b6a924b104f" :answer-field/key "field-